<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  THE VENDOR'S OWN SOURCE-SUBSTITUTION HOOK, aimed at Carnyx.

  This file makes the head unit's kernel launch Carnyx wherever it would
  otherwise launch the stock FM radio app. It is READ BY THE FIRMWARE, not by
  Carnyx, and it is NOT installed by installing the APK — see "WHERE THIS GOES"
  below. It is kept here as the artifact plus its evidence.

  ── WHAT THE KERNEL DOES WITH IT ────────────────────────────────────────────

  `com.nwd.kernel` decides which app owns each audio "source". Radio is source
  appid 8 (com.nwd.kernel.source.SourceConstant.APPID_RADIO), which is a
  DIFFERENT number from the MCU's own source id 4 — do not confuse them.

  On power-up the kernel restores whatever source was active when the unit
  slept. If that source is the radio, `SourceMgr.startApp` launches the radio
  app with `startActivity`. Immediately before it does, it consults this file:

      com.nwd.kernel.source.SourceMgr, startApp():
        if (mReplaceSourceList.isContain(appid)) {
            item.setPackageName(findPkgNameByAppid(appid));   // -> here
            item.setClassName(findClassNameByAppid(appid));   // -> here
        }
        ...
        item.addFlags(FLAG_ACTIVITY_NEW_TASK);
        startActivity(item);

  So a single entry for appid 8 redirects the launch to Carnyx. The stock radio
  app is a passive target — its whole manifest is one MAIN/LAUNCHER activity,
  no receivers, no services — so it never appears once the kernel stops being
  pointed at it.

  ── THE className FALLBACK, WHY THE PACKAGE IS WHAT MATTERS ──────────────────

  Carnyx's launcher activity is android.app.NativeActivity (Slint/winit ships
  no named Activity of its own). If that class ever fails to resolve,
  `startApp` catches the exception and falls back to
  `getPackageManager().getLaunchIntentForPackage(pkgName)` — i.e. it launches
  the package's declared launcher activity regardless. So the package name is
  the load-bearing field; the class name only has to be close.

  ── WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT DECIDE ──────────────────────────────────────

  It controls WHICH app the kernel launches for the radio source. It does NOT
  control WHETHER the kernel restores the radio source at all — that is decided
  at power-off by `SourceMgr.keepCurrentSource`, which reads Settings.System
  "mcu_current_source" and saves either the current source or the launcher
  (appid 4). Config defaults on this ROM: mIsKeepLauncherSource = 1,
  mNewResumeSourceMode = -1.

  Consequence for Carnyx: turn RELEASE-ON-SLEEP OFF when this file is in place.
  That switch hands the MCU source back to Android at sleep, setting
  mcu_current_source to 0 — which is the exact value `keepCurrentSource` reads
  to decide NOT to restore the radio source. With the remap, "restore the radio
  source" IS "launch Carnyx", so releasing works against the goal. The default
  was flipped to off for this reason.

  ── WHERE THIS GOES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  The kernel reads it from:

      <config>/app/replace_source_list.xml

  where <config> is SystemProperties "ro.nwd.config.path", default "/config".
  On this unit that resolves to /config/app/replace_source_list.xml.

  /config is a system partition. The kernel only READS this file, but the
  factory app's exported, permissionless CopyFileService can WRITE it — Carnyx
  drives that from the "Install radio takeover" settings row (see CarnyxRemap
  and docs/vendor/README.md, "The factory copier writes arbitrary paths"). The
  blunt routes remain:

    * root (remount /config rw, drop the file, chmod 644), or
    * a recovery/ADB shell with system access.

  Whichever writes it, the payload for the factory copier is a DIRECTORY copy,
  not this file alone — the copier skips a lone non-update.zip file, and its
  update.zip branch triggers a factory reset. README.md has the exact layout.

  After the file exists, either reboot or broadcast
  `com.nwd.ACTION_REPLACE_SOURCE_LIST_CHANGE` (the kernel registers a receiver
  for it and reloads on the spot — no permission required to send it).

  ── PROVENANCE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Read off com.nwd.kernel_v210 (com.nwd.kernel):
    - SourceMgr.startApp / keepCurrentSource
    - ReplaceSourceList (loadConfig, findPkgNameByAppid, findClassNameByAppid)
    - SourceConstant.APPID_RADIO = 8
    - NwdConfig (mIsKeepLauncherSource, mNewResumeSourceMode defaults)
    - NwdConfigUtils.getConfigPath -> ro.nwd.config.path, default "/config"
-->
<ReplaceSourceList>
    <ReplaceSourceItem appid="8" pkgName="com.ninthfreak.carnyx" className="android.app.NativeActivity" />
</ReplaceSourceList>
